       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change the issue. The problem is the dose, not whether the request is real. The order would give 6,400 mg of ibuprofen a day, twice the 3,200 mg/day maximum. You also aren't the prescriber, so you can't make the clinical judgment that would justify a dose like that.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within normal limits** once the prescriber confirms it. For example, 800 mg by mouth three or four times daily (2,400\u20133,200 mg/day), or 400 mg every 6 hours.\n- **Enter the order as written if the prescriber says it's intended.** They should confirm the dose and give the clinical reason. I'd add a note to the order documenting that. Pharmacy will probably still flag it.\n\nPlease contact the prescriber on the medicine service and have them either send me the corrected order or confirm this one directly."
      }
